# Build config. The SDK auto-discovers ./source and ./resources by convention,
# INCLUDING resource qualifiers like ./resources-<device> and ./resources-spa, so
# pointing at the manifest is enough.
#
# Launcher icons: each device has its own resources-<device>/drawables/ with a
# correctly-sized icon plus its own drawable definition (auto-discovered by the
# device qualifier). There is deliberately NO icon in the base resources/ -- a base
# icon would be overridden by every device and the packager would warn about it. The
# base resources/ holds only shared, size-independent resources (strings).
#
# The launcher icons are this app's OWN (no longer the placeholders copied from Option A
# that an earlier version of this comment described): a cobalt ring with the amber average
# line and the white arrow crossing it, drawn flat at each size by store/gen_icon.py. See
# SPEC 3.3 for how they were made and why the launchers are smooth while the 1024 master
# and the 500x500 store icon keep the tyre knobs.
project.manifest = manifest.xml
